{%- comment -%}
  The app mirrors its already-obfuscated storefront script into app-owned shop
  metafields (`script`, `script_2` ... `script_6`; `script_parts` says how many
  are valid). They are printed here as ONE inline <script>: no network request,
  no app server on the shopper path, runs as soon as the parser reaches it.

  Target `compliance_head` is the earliest app-embed slot Shopify documents.
  For first-byte-in-head delivery the app also writes
  `snippets/pagepulse-head-inline.liquid` and a `{% render %}` immediately
  after `<head>` in `layout/theme.liquid` (see theme-head-inject.server.ts).
  When that path is active, `theme_head_active` is true and this embed prints
  nothing (avoids double execution).

  There is deliberately NO <script src> fallback and NO else branch.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless app.metafields.pagepulse.theme_head_active -%}
{% render 'pagepulse-inline' %}
{%- endunless -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Performance Script Loader",
  "target": "compliance_head",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
